  "kind": "build",
  "title": "# Build: notes-views (Opus, medium thinking) **Name:** Notes views · **Category:** Feature ## What …",
  "asked": "# Build: notes-views (Opus, medium thinking) **Name:** Notes views · **Category:** Feature ## What Brett said (verbatim, Nov 4 2026, voice) \"Make the sections in your note collapsible.\" (Asked: just this note or every note?) \"Yeah, make a couple of views. One view is the same way it is now, but with collapsible sections, and another view is the notes in a grid with expandable rows that shows the note.\" Context: the console's **Notes** screen (console_show target 'notes') shows AmberX notes/to-dos/tasks (amberx.items). Amber just saved a long note, 'Features that landed: Nov 3-4 2026', with sections in caps (JUST MERGED / NOV 4 (EARLIER) / OVERNIGHT BATCH) and bullet lists. Use it as the test case. Book to a free named agent. Create a Plan Studio plan for this build (name + category above). ## Do 1. **A view switcher** on the Notes screen (toolbar asset, remembered per device; also in View menu, right-click, voice/API/MCP/CLI): - **Classic (default):** today's layout, but every note body renders **collapsible sections**: Markdown headings (#, ##, ###) and ALL-CAPS lines ending a paragraph (like 'JUST MERGED (...)') become fold headers with a chevron and an item count. Expand all / Collapse all per note, remember the fold state per note per device, and keep search hits auto-expanded and highlighted. - **Grid:** notes as rows (title, kind, list, tags, priority, due, updated, created, section count, length), sortable on every column with filters, search and right-click column hiding. **Tapping a row expands it** to show the full note rendered with the same collapsible sections, plus Edit / Open / Pin / Move / Delete actions. Multi-expand is allowed, and a phone layout as cards. 2. Shared collapsible-section renderer component (framework level, reusable by Plan Studio/MD Studio later), AXF tokens only, accessible (keyboard, aria-expanded). 3. The same views in the AmberX app's notes screen if it shares the component. If not, record a follow-up rather than editing Android (Android hold). 4. Settings through the framework settings interface (default view, auto-detect caps headings on/off, start collapsed/expanded). Basic docs/README.md note, tests, phone + desktop UI Review shots (non-blocking). 5. PR **through the merge queue only** (auto-land is OFF). Report in _claude/builds/reports/. Commits clean. Watch live: Brett can watch the screen you are changing hot-render in the console. Whenever you start work on a screen or element, run `node framework/cli/axf.mjs focus <app> [route] [css-selector] --note \"<what you are changing>\"` (apps: console-web, axhub-web, amberx-droid, walkthrough-studio, demo, framework, console, axhub-android, voicevault). Agent cap: heavy steps (pnpm/npm/vite builds, docker node:22 test runs, Playwright) share a VPS-wide lock. Run each one as `node /opt/axf/deploy/../framework/cli/agent-slots.mjs heavy -- <command>` so only a few run at once. Model switches (Brett, Nov 3 2026): a downgrade (e.g. Fable → Opus) is fine. An UPGRADE (e.g. Opus → Fable) needs Brett's approval: when you reach one, run `node apps/console-web/plugins/build-orchestrator/orchestrator.mjs request-upgrade <id> <phase>`, ask once, and stop. Never approve a model switch upgrade yourself (no `act approve` on an upgrade), never relaunch on a higher model.",
